-- title:
--   Monodromy orbits upstairs match automorphism orbits downstairs
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $j_0$ be an element of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`. Write $H = \mathrm{HahnSeries}\ \mathbb{Q}\ \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ for the field of Hahn series with rational exponents and coefficients in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and let $E_{\mathrm{near}} =$ `nearCurve j₀` be the Weierstrass curve `WeierstrassCurve.ofJ` over $H$ attached to the invariant $j_0 + t$, where $t$ is the Hahn series with single term of exponent $1$ and coefficient $1$; downstairs let $E_0 =$ `WeierstrassCurve.ofJ j₀` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. The type `CycSubH (nearCurve j₀) p` consists of additive subgroups $G$ of the affine point group of $E_{\mathrm{near}}$ for which there is a point $g$ of additive order exactly $p$ with $G = \mathbb{Z}g$, and `CycSub E₀ p` is the analogous type of subgroups $\mathbb{Z}g$ of the point group of $E_0$ generated by a point of additive order $p$. The assertion is that there exists a bijection $\beta$ between these two types such that, for all $G, G'$ in `CycSubH (nearCurve j₀) p`, the following are equivalent: (i) there is an element $m$ of [`HahnSeries.monodromy Qbar`](def/HahnSeries_Monodromy.html#L121) — the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphisms of $H$ that is the image under `hahnTwistHom` of the group of characters $\chi : \mathrm{Multiplicative}\ \mathbb{Q} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}^{\times}$ with $\chi(1) = 1$, $\chi$ acting on a Hahn series by multiplying its coefficient at exponent $a$ by $\chi(a)$ — with `b3Act j₀ m G.1 = G'.1`, i.e. the image of $G$ under the additive automorphism of the points of $E_{\mathrm{near}}$ obtained by transporting points along $m$ (which carries $E_{\mathrm{near}}$ to itself) is $G'$; (ii) `SameOrbit E₀ (β G).1 (β G').1`, i.e. there is a variable change $\gamma$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\gamma \bullet E_0 = E_0$ and points $g, g'$ of $E_0$ with $(\beta G).1 = \mathbb{Z}g$, $(\beta G').1 = \mathbb{Z}g'$ and $g'$ equal, as a heterogeneous equality, to the image `Point.vcInvFun γ E₀.toAffine g` of $g$ on $\gamma \bullet E_0$.
--
--   This is the specialisation bridge for cyclic subgroups of order $p$: it transfers the monodromy action on order-$p$ subgroups of the near curve over the Hahn series field to the action of the automorphisms (variable changes preserving the curve) on order-$p$ subgroups of the curve with invariant $j_0$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the two equivalence relations corresponding under some bijection of the two sets of subgroups. It is used in the construction of an elliptic curve together with a cyclic subgroup of prime order in a prescribed orbit, [`ModularCurve.exists_elliptic_cycSub_orbitMap_prime_of_ne_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_elliptic_cycSub_orbitMap_prime_of_ne_two); note that no canonicity of $\beta$ is asserted, only its existence and compatibility with the two relations.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_B3_b3_specialisationEquivariance.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_SpecialisationBridge

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open ModularCurve ModularCurve.TatePoint ModularCurve.B3

theorem ModularCurve.B3.b3_specialisationEquivariance (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] [NeZero p] (j₀ : Qbar) :
    ∃ β : CycSubH (nearCurve j₀) p ≃ CycSub (WeierstrassCurve.ofJ j₀) p,
      ∀ G G' : CycSubH (nearCurve j₀) p,
        (∃ m : HahnSeries.monodromy Qbar, b3Act j₀ m G.1 = G'.1) ↔
          SameOrbit (WeierstrassCurve.ofJ j₀) (β G).1 (β G').1 := by sorry
